# vendor/ stays listed here ON PURPOSE even though the production tree IS
# committed. The production host (cPanel, arm.sdvunf.uz) has no composer and no
# outbound network, so `git pull` is the only way dependencies can reach it, and
# the tree is force-added (`git add -f vendor`) by tools/build-vendor.php.
#
# Keeping the ignore rule is what makes that workable day to day: files already
# tracked are unaffected by it, while the dev-only packages a plain
# `composer install` adds afterwards (pest, phpunit, dusk, faker, pint...) stay
# ignored and can never leak into a release.
# See CLAUDE.md, section "Bogʻliqliklar (vendor) — git orqali".
/vendor
.env
.env.backup
.env.production
.phpactor.json
.phpunit.result.cache
